From: SheepyLord <37598021+SheepyLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 10:56:20 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Atmosphere: the night sky editor: each layer on its own, the
 constellations apart

The GMod native loader's night sky editor (its ADR 0227) gives each element of the night sky its own
look. The night sky image is four layers the sky adds in gamma space, as Skyrim adds its sky layers:
the stars, the constellations' bright stars, the galaxy band and the nebulae. Each now has a
brightness (rtx.atmosphere.starMap{Star,Constellation,Galaxy,Nebula}Brightness, 0-8, a multiple of the
image's) and a colour (...Saturation, 0 grey, 1 the image's, 2 twice as strong). A brightness becomes
the gamma-space weight brightness^(1/2.2), so a layer alone scales by its brightness once decoded; the
sum is held at 1 as before, or at the brightest weight above it; at the defaults the image is as it
was (rtx_night_sky_layers.h, tests/rtx/unit/test_night_sky_layers.cpp).

The constellations' bright stars were baked into the nebula texture. They are a layer of their own
now, in the nebula's mapping: the file beside the nebula's named <name>_constellations.dds (binding
222, AtmosphereStarMapConstellations), so no new path option reaches Lua. They come out with the stars
in the twilight; the galaxy and the nebulae still wait for deep night.

A layer at brightness 0 is neither drawn nor kept: its texture is freed, and loaded again when turned
up. SKY_TEXTURE_NIGHT_IMAGE now chooses the image's night, so with every layer off the night has no
stars rather than the procedural field, which stays only while no layer's file loads.

The shooting stars' fixed 8 % of four-second slots is now rtx.atmosphere.shootingStarsPerMinute (1.2,
the same; 0-15) and their brightness rtx.atmosphere.shootingStarBrightness (1, 0-8).

The new arguments are three 16-byte rows at the end of AtmosphereArgs, per pixel only:
normalizeForSkyLutCache zeroes them, so no bake re-runs when they change. RtxOptions.md has the new
rows and the changed descriptions of starMapEnable and starMapNebulaTexture.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
